+# Rekor Restore Drill — Operational Playbook
+
+Overview
+- Validate full DB restore from backups, validate Rekor server integrity, rotate TLS certs and test client validation.
+
+Pre-reqs
+- Access to backup bucket (s3://aegis-rekor-backups).
+- Staging Postgres / RDS sandbox.
+- Rekor staging deployment and DNS entries (rekor.staging.internal).
+
+Steps
+1. Find latest backup:
+   aws s3 ls s3://aegis-rekor-backups/ --summarize | tail -n 1
+2. Download:
+   aws s3 cp s3://aegis-rekor-backups/<file> /tmp/rekor.dump
+3. Restore:
+   PGPASSWORD=${STAGING_PG_PASSWORD} pg_restore -h ${STAGING_PG_HOST} -U ${STAGING_PG_USER} -d rekor --clean /tmp/rekor.dump
+4. Update Rekor config:
+   Point Rekor deployment to staging DB connection string; update K8s Secret rekor-db; rollout restart deployment/rekor-server
+5. Validate API:
+   curl -sSk https://rekor.staging.internal/api/v1/log/log_info | jq .
+6. Test signed entry write/read:
+   Use rekor CLI or client: push a test entry and verify retrieval.
+
+TLS Cert Rotation
+1. Issue cert from internal CA or cert-manager.
+2. Apply new TLS secret:
+   kubectl -n rekor create secret tls rekor-tls --cert=rekor.crt --key=rekor.key --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
+3. Restart and validate.
+
+Post-Drill
+- Document time-to-restore, data differences, and runbook gaps.
+- Store report in DR binder and notify stakeholders.
+
