+# BYOK & Private Endpoint Runbook — LLM Vendors
+
+Purpose
+- Ensure LLM API calls traverse vendor private endpoints and that keys (if supported) remain under customer control (BYOK).
+
+General Steps
+1. Legal & Procurement
+   - Execute DPA and BYOK clauses with vendor. Get vendor steps/contacts for key import and private endpoint.
+2. Network & VPC
+   - Provision Private Service Connect (GCP) / PrivateLink (AWS) / Anthropic private network per vendor docs.
+   - Ensure k8s pods can reach VPC endpoints via ENIs or VPC egress setup (NAT/Gateway/Workload Identity).
+3. BYOK Key Import
+   - Create KMS key (Customer-managed) in your cloud and follow vendor import steps (often upload public key/certificate).
+   - Verify vendor acknowledges key and test encryption flows (if vendor supports EKM/BYOK).
+4. Adapter configuration
+   - Set OPENAI_API_BASE / ANTHROPIC_API_BASE / AIP_API_ENDPOINT to vendor private endpoints in k8s secret (ops/llm/private_endpoint_example.yaml).
+   - Update adapter to use these endpoints and verify traffic path using tcpdump or flow logs.
+5. Test & Validate
+   - Run integration tests and ensure no calls go to public APIs (use egress firewall rules temporarily).
+   - Validate that vendor does not retain training rights if DPA prohibits it.
+
+Vendor-specific notes
+- OpenAI: request private endpoint access via account manager; support for org-level private endpoints + private conversations exists on some plans.
+- Anthropic: request private network/private endpoint and BYOK support where offered.
+- Google: use Private Service Connect and Vertex AI private endpoints + Workload Identity.
