+# OpenTelemetry Instrumentation Guidelines for Aegis
+
+Goals
+- Capture traces for requests crossing MCP, Kafka producers/consumers, Rekor writes, and LLM adapter calls.
+- Export to centralized OTLP collector (observability/otel-collector.yaml).
+
+Instrumentation patterns
+- FastAPI: use opentelemetry-instrumentation-fastapi + ASGI middleware and automatic instrumentation for requests.
+- Kafka: add tracing to produce/consume with opentelemetry-instrumentation-confluent-kafka or manual propagate headers.
+- Rekor: instrument HTTP client calls to Rekor and record traces for write/read operations.
+- LLM Adapter: instrument prompt->response pipeline and RAG retrieval latency, and persist trace_id in MCP evidence bundle for correlation.
+
+Trace sampling & retention
+- Set adaptive sampling for production (e.g., 1% default with higher sampling for errors / high-sensitivity calls).
+- Configure retention & storage in observability backend (e.g., Tempo/Jaeger/GCP Trace).
+
+Correlation
+- Ensure logs include trace_id and span_id (e.g., structured JSON logging).
+- Export metrics derived from traces (p95 tail latencies).
+
