+# Kafka Production Monitoring & DLQ Runbook
+
+Objectives
+- Monitor cluster health, consumer lag, broker disk utilization, DLQ backlog, and provide operator run procedures.
+
+Metrics to monitor
+- broker: CPU, memory, disk, under-replicated partitions
+- consumer: consumer_lag per consumer group
+- DLQ: backlog size and retry success rate
+- Connectors: connector task failures
+
+Alerts
+- Under-replicated partitions > 0 for 5m -> page
+- Consumer lag > threshold for 10m -> page
+- DLQ retry failure rate > 5% in 15m -> page
+
+Procedures
+1. Investigate alert, check metrics and logs (kubectl logs / broker metrics).
+2. If consumer lag: check consumer group offset, restart consumer, scale consumer replicas.
+3. If broker disk pressure: add storage or scale brokers (run strimzi resize with care).
+4. For DLQ: inspect top messages, run dlq_consumer_improved.py locally to reprocess; deadlettered files in S3 for forensics.
